{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Noah","id":"360967589511561218","is_bot":0,"username":"king.crusader"},"author_id":"360967589511561218","channel_id":"638590342005784588","content":"```The Wendigo was gaunt to the point of emaciation, its desiccated skin pulled tautly over its bones. With its bones pushing out against its skin, its complexion the ash gray of death, and its eyes pushed back deep into their sockets, the Wendigo looked like a gaunt skeleton recently disinterred from the grave. What lips it had were tattered and bloody. Its body was unclean and suffering from suppuration of the flesh, giving off a strange and eerie odor of decay and decomposition, of death and corruption.  - Kragheim Shieldblazen```\n\n\nIn some traditions, Wendigos were created when a human resorted to cannibalism to survive. Other sources say that they originated from a lost Arcanian race corrupted by time. These creatures make up a skeletal and furred beast oozing bits of gore that it has consumed and made part of itself. Legends sprawl across the realm of all different breeds. In Arcania, Wendigos are considered some of the most terrifying creatures to exist in the wilderness, able to confuse the weary traveller by mimicrying familiar voices before luring them to their deaths. Their insatiable hunger can be heard in their nightly feastings; the terrible screeching of animals caught in the middle of the night. Most will never even see one before it pounces and rips them apart. Pray to the gods that you never encounter such a beast.","created_at":"2020-08-10T08:23:24.592000Z","edited_at":"2020-08-10T08:23:50.356000Z","id":"742297035989843988","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
